ue] [17592186484797 1077 "field-1" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484797 1078 #edb/ref 17592186484790 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484797 1079 #uuid "f03b9128-e960-5087-b4b2-f78af1a3ef3c" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484798 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186064284.py" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484798 1169 #uuid "33d29e3d-bb12-5c9e-a20a-5ea0e9d6624e" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484799 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484795 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484799 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484799 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484799 1072 #uuid "30a0323d-00da-5727-8bed-8f4570018874" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484799 1074 "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{4})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4})=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} x}{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$$" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484800 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484796 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484800 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484800 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484800 1072 #uuid "53218be1-6a3c-5560-9338-ef81bd9ab181" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484800 1074 "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{6})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{6})=- \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$$" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484801 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484793 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484801 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484801 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484801 1072 #uuid "9c2a70b8-20d0-5b7c-a81b-d0ca3277e712" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484801 1074 "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{3}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{3})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{3})=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)(x-0),\\qquad y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{3} x}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}.$$" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484802 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484797 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484802 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484802 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\cos{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)}$ at the point $\\left(0,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$.\n\nWrite the right-hand side of the equation in terms of $x$.\n\n$y=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484802 1072 #uuid "cfc21866-9683-5244-ad3b-eca7c1a8e833" 13194139535244 17592186045443 true] [17592186484802 1074 "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=0$ is given by $f'(0)$.\n\nWe calculate $f'(x)$ using the chain rule. First, express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$f=\\cos u,\\qquad u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4}.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=-\\sin u,\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\cos x.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule:\n\n$$f'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-\\sin(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{\\pi}{4})\\cos x.$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives $f'(0)=-\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{4})=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$.\n\nFinally, use the point-slope equation:\n\n$$y-\\lef